/**
\mainpage Qore PDF Module

\section intro Introduction

The `pdf` module provides PDF functionality for Qore using QPDF and PoDoFo,
with optional PDFium support for rendering and text extraction.

\section features Features

- Create PDFs with PoDoFo
- Read/edit/merge/split PDFs with QPDF
- Optional rendering and text extraction with PDFium
- Data provider actions for Qorus integration via @ref pdfdataprovider "PdfDataProvider"

\section pdfdataprovider PdfDataProvider Module

The @ref PdfDataProvider::PdfDataProvider "PdfDataProvider" module provides integration with Qore's
DataProvider API. See the <a href="../../PdfDataProvider/html/index.html">PdfDataProvider module documentation</a>
for complete API reference.

\section dataprov Data Provider Actions

The module ships with PdfDataProvider for Qore's data provider framework.
Example `qdp` commands:

\code{.bash}
qdp 'pdf{}/document/create' output_path=out.pdf,page_count=2
qdp 'pdf{}/document/info' input_path=out.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/metadata' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=meta.pdf,metadata='{"title":"Updated"}'
qdp 'pdf{}/document/merge' inputs='("a.pdf","b.pdf")',output_path=merged.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/rotate' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=rotated.pdf,pages='(0)',degrees=90
qdp 'pdf{}/render/page' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0,dpi=150
qdp 'pdf{}/render/extract-text' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0
\endcode

\section dependencies Dependencies

- QPDF (required)
- PoDoFo (required; bundled by default, LGPL-2.0-or-later)
- PDFium (optional)

\section packages OS Packages

The bundled PoDoFo build requires common graphics/font libraries. PDFium is
optional; there is no MacPorts PDFium port.

\subsection packages_ubuntu Ubuntu

\code{.bash}
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y \
  cmake pkg-config qpdf libqpdf-dev libfreetype-dev \
  libssl-dev libxml2-dev libfontconfig1-dev libpng-dev \
  libjpeg-turbo8-dev libtiff-dev zlib1g-dev
\endcode

PDFium (optional): not packaged in standard Ubuntu repos; provide a prebuilt
`libpdfium` and pass `-DENABLE_PDFIUM=ON -DPDFIUM_INCLUDE_DIR=... -DPDFIUM_LIBRARY=...`,
or use `-DENABLE_PDFIUM=OFF`.

\subsection packages_alpine Alpine

\code{.bash}
sudo apk add --no-cache \
  cmake pkgconfig qpdf qpdf-dev freetype-dev \
  openssl-dev libxml2-dev fontconfig-dev libpng-dev \
  libjpeg-turbo-dev tiff-dev zlib-dev
\endcode

PDFium (optional): not in Alpine repos; provide a prebuilt `libpdfium` and pass
`-DENABLE_PDFIUM=ON -DPDFIUM_INCLUDE_DIR=... -DPDFIUM_LIBRARY=...`,
or use `-DENABLE_PDFIUM=OFF`.

\subsection packages_fedora Fedora

\code{.bash}
sudo dnf install -y \
  cmake pkgconf-pkg-config qpdf qpdf-devel freetype-devel \
  openssl-devel libxml2-devel fontconfig-devel libpng-devel \
  libjpeg-turbo-devel libtiff-devel zlib-devel
\endcode

\subsection packages_macports MacPorts

\code{.bash}
sudo port install \
  cmake pkgconfig qpdf freetype openssl3 libxml2 fontconfig libpng \
  libjpeg-turbo tiff zlib
\endcode

\section pdfreleasenotes_link Release Notes

See \subpage pdfreleasenotes for release notes and version history.

